# Create Terraform Module — GCP

Scaffolds a new `{{MODULE_PREFIX}}-{name}` directory following workspace conventions.

## When to Use
- Creating a new GCP resource module from scratch
- Generating boilerplate for a new module repo
- Adding standard files (tests, examples, pre-commit) to an existing module

## Prerequisites
- Module name (lowercase, hyphenated)
- Primary GCP resource type(s)
- Optional features needed (Private Service Connect, KMS encryption, IAM bindings)

## Procedure

### 1. Gather Requirements
Ask for:
- Module name: used as `{{MODULE_PREFIX}}-{name}`
- Primary resource(s) to manage
- Optional features: {{OPTIONAL_FEATURES}}
<!-- Example GCP features: private_service_connect, kms_encryption, iam_bindings, vpc_peering -->

### 2. Create Directory Structure
```
{{MODULE_PREFIX}}-{name}/
├── main.tf                    # Provider requirements + data sources
├── {resource}.tf              # Core resource(s)
├── locals.tf                  # Name construction, label merging
├── variables.tf               # Module-specific variables
├── {{COMMON_VARS_FILE}}       # Standard cross-module variables
├── outputs.tf                 # Module outputs
├── versions.tf                # Version constraints
├── README.md                  # Documentation
├── .pre-commit-config.yaml    # Validation hooks
├── .tflint.hcl                # TFLint rules
├── .terraform-docs.yml        # Doc generation
├── examples/
│   └── basic/
│       ├── main.tf
│       └── variables.tf
└── tests/
    └── {resource}.tftest.hcl  # Native terraform tests
```

### 3. File Templates

#### versions.tf
```hcl
terraform {
  required_version = ">=1.3"
  required_providers {
    google = {
      source  = "hashicorp/google"
      version = ">=5.0,<6.0"
    }
  }
}
```

#### locals.tf — Naming and Label Pattern
```hcl
locals {
  {{NAMING_LOCALS}}
  # Labels: defaults + resource-specific, resource-specific wins
  # GCP labels: lowercase, max 63 chars, alphanumeric + dashes + underscores
  labels = merge(var.env_default_labels, var.labels)
}
```

#### common.variables.tf — Standard Cross-Module Variables
```hcl
variable "prefix" {
  type        = string
  description = "Resource name prefix."
}

variable "project_id" {
  type        = string
  description = "GCP project ID."
}

variable "region" {
  type        = string
  description = "GCP region."
}

variable "labels" {
  type        = map(string)
  default     = {}
  description = "Additional resource labels (take precedence over env_default_labels on conflict)."
}

variable "env_default_labels" {
  type        = map(string)
  default     = {}
  description = "Default labels from the orchestration layer."
}
```

#### Resource file pattern
```hcl
resource "{{PROVIDER_RESOURCE}}" "default" {
  name       = local.name
  project    = var.project_id
  {{LOCATION_ATTRIBUTE}}

  labels = local.labels

  # Resource-specific configuration...
}
```

#### outputs.tf
```hcl
output "name" {
  value       = {{PROVIDER_RESOURCE}}.default.name
  description = "Name of the resource."
}

output "id" {
  value       = {{PROVIDER_RESOURCE}}.default.id
  description = "The ID of the resource."
}

output "self_link" {
  value       = {{PROVIDER_RESOURCE}}.default.self_link
  description = "The self-link URI of the resource."
}
```

#### Test file pattern
```hcl
mock_provider "google" {}

override_data {
  target = data.google_project.current
  values = {
    project_id = "test-project-123"
    number     = 123456789
    name       = "test-project"
  }
}

variables {
  prefix             = "test-auto"
  project_id         = "test-project-123"
  region             = "europe-west1"
  labels             = {}
  env_default_labels = { managed_by = "terraform" }
}

run "creates_resource_with_correct_name" {
  command = plan
  assert {
    condition     = {{PROVIDER_RESOURCE}}.default.name == "{{EXPECTED_NAME_PATTERN}}"
    error_message = "Name should follow naming convention"
  }
}

run "merges_labels_correctly" {
  command = plan
  variables {
    labels = { extra = "label" }
  }
  assert {
    condition     = {{PROVIDER_RESOURCE}}.default.labels["extra"] == "label"
    error_message = "Custom labels should be merged"
  }
}
```

### 4. Post-Creation
1. `terraform fmt -recursive`
2. `terraform validate`
3. `terraform test`
4. `terraform-docs` to generate README
